  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A trough of low pressure will move\neastward across the Silver State this morning, resulting in light\nprecipitation in Northern Elko County. The snow level will be\naround 5,000 feet. Precipitation amounts will be below one tenth\nof an inch. The majority of this precipitation will remain north\nof Interstate 80. A ridge of high pressure will build northward\nacross Nevada Tuesday through Friday. This will result in a\nwarming trend. By Friday afternoon, high temperatures throughout\nNorthern and Central Nevada will be around ten degrees above\nnormal for this time of year. Here are probabilities of maximum\ntemperatures of 55 degrees or higher for select locations in\nNorthern and Central Nevada on Friday, November 27th, 2026:\n\nGabbs - 97%\nTonopah - 96%\nBattle Mountain - 85%\nCarlin - 65%\nWinnemucca - 55%\nEly - 55%\nLund - 55%\nElko - 40%\nEureka - 30%\nSpring Creek - 20%\n\nHigh temperatures will remain well above seasonal values\nSaturday afternoon. Precipitation ahead of the next storm system\nmay overspread Northern Nevada Sunday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding light precipitation in Northern Elko County this\nmorning. High forecast confidence in a warming trend Tuesday\nthrough Friday. Low forecast confidence in the next storm system\nimpacting Northern Nevada Sunday.",
